---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import ProcessImage from '../../../components/ProcessImage.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Secondary Processes for CNC Machined Parts" description="Grinding, heat treatment, surface finishing and other secondary process support coordinated through Belaro Precision's Dongguan and Shenzhen supplier network.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero secondary-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/services/">Capabilities</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Secondary Processes</span></nav>
        <div class="secondary-media-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">SECONDARY PROCESS SUPPORT / DONGGUAN &amp; SHENZHEN</span><h1>Beyond machining.<br/><em>Coordinated around your part.</em></h1><p>Belaro can coordinate grinding, heat treatment, surface finishing and other required secondary processes through the manufacturing ecosystems and supplier networks in Dongguan and Shenzhen.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-orange" href="/contact/#rfq-form">Discuss your requirements <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link text-link-light" href="#processes">Explore processes <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div><ProcessImage loading="eager" name="secondary-processes" alt="Grinding, anodizing, coating, heat treatment, blasting and polishing process examples" width={1586} height={992} /></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section"><div class="container secondary-position"><div><span class="eyebrow">ONE COORDINATED REQUIREMENT</span><h2>Machining is often only<br/><em>one step in the route.</em></h2></div><div><p class="lead">A finished component may need additional processing before it is ready for assembly or service.</p><p>Based in Shenzhen, we draw on the manufacturing ecosystems and supplier networks in Dongguan and Shenzhen. This enables flexible support beyond CNC machining while keeping the drawing, process requirements and commercial scope aligned around one part.</p><p>Secondary processes are reviewed and coordinated per project. Specific suppliers, process standards, certificates, inspection methods and lead times are confirmed during quotation rather than assumed from this page.</p></div></div></section>

    <section class="section section-soft" id="processes"><div class="container"><SectionHeading eyebrow="PROCESS OPTIONS" title="Support for the route your drawing requires" text="The exact route depends on material, geometry, dimensional requirements and the applicable process specification."/><div class="process-grid"><article id="grinding"><span>01 / PROCESS</span><h3>Grinding</h3><p>Grinding requirements can be coordinated where a drawing calls for an additional finishing step after machining.</p><ul><li>Identify the surfaces to be ground</li><li>State the final dimensions and tolerances</li><li>Define surface finish and datum requirements</li><li>Confirm inspection after grinding</li></ul></article><article id="heat-treatment"><span>02 / PROCESS</span><h3>Heat Treatment</h3><p>Heat treatment can be reviewed against the specified material condition, hardness requirement and applicable standard.</p><ul><li>Provide the material grade and condition</li><li>State the treatment and hardness requirement</li><li>Identify distortion-sensitive features</li><li>List any required records or test evidence</li></ul></article><article id="surface-finishing"><span>03 / PROCESS</span><h3>Surface Finishing</h3><p>Surface finishing is coordinated according to the drawing callout and the functional or cosmetic needs of the component.</p><ul><li>Provide the finish or coating specification</li><li>Mark masking and contact areas</li><li>Identify dimensions affected by coating thickness</li><li>Define appearance or acceptance criteria</li></ul></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="container other-processes"><div><span class="eyebrow">OTHER SECONDARY PROCESSES</span><h2>Share the complete drawing,<br/><em>not just the machining model.</em></h2></div><div><p>Other post-machining operations may also be reviewed through the local manufacturing network. Availability is not presented as a fixed catalogue because the appropriate supplier and route depend on the part, material, specification, quantity and quality requirements.</p><p>Include every required process in your RFQ. Belaro will clarify what can be coordinated, what documentation is available and which responsibilities form part of the quotation.</p><a class="text-link" href="/machined-parts/">Explore machined part families <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>

    <section class="section section-soft"><div class="container"><SectionHeading eyebrow="RFQ CHECKLIST" title="Define the final part condition" text="Clear requirements help determine the process route and the checks needed after each operation."/><dl class="requirements-list"><div><dt>Material & starting condition</dt><dd>Exact grade, temper or condition, plus any material documentation required.</dd></div><div><dt>Process specification</dt><dd>The named treatment, finish or standard, including hardness, coating or surface requirements where applicable.</dd></div><div><dt>Final dimensions</dt><dd>Dimensions and tolerances that apply after grinding, heat treatment or surface finishing.</dd></div><div><dt>Protected areas</dt><dd>Masking, threads, sealing faces, electrical contact areas or surfaces that must remain untreated.</dd></div><div><dt>Inspection & records</dt><dd>Critical checks, hardness or finish evidence, certificates and reporting expectations.</dd></div><div><dt>Quantity & delivery</dt><dd>Batch quantity, repeat demand and target delivery so the complete route can be reviewed.</dd></div></dl></div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="container secondary-faq"><SectionHeading eyebrow="BEFORE YOU ENQUIRE" title="Secondary process questions"/><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Are all secondary processes completed in-house?</summary><p>No. Belaro's core offering is CNC machining. Grinding, heat treatment, surface finishing and other secondary processes may be coordinated through suitable suppliers in the Dongguan and Shenzhen manufacturing network, with scope confirmed per project.</p></details><details><summary>Can you manage machining and finishing as one requirement?</summary><p>Yes, the complete process route can be reviewed from one drawing and RFQ. The quotation will clarify the included operations, specifications, inspection and delivery scope.</p></details><details><summary>What information should I add to the drawing?</summary><p>State the process specification, final dimensions, surface or hardness requirements, masking areas, acceptance criteria and any documents needed with the order.</p></details><details><summary>Can you provide certificates or test records?</summary><p>List the exact records required in your enquiry. Availability and format depend on the selected process, supplier and agreed project scope.</p></details></div></div></section>

    <section class="cta-section"><div class="container cta-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">COMPLETE PROCESS REQUIREMENT</span><h2>Let’s review the route<br/><em>for your finished part.</em></h2><p>Send the drawing, process specifications, quantity and requested records for a project-specific review.</p></div><a class="button button-orange button-large" href="/contact/#rfq-form">Request a Quote <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .breadcrumbs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-bottom:38px;font-size:13px;color:#c7d1dd}.breadcrumbs a:hover{color:var(--orange)}
  @media(max-width:700px){.breadcrumbs{margin-bottom:28px}}
  .secondary-media-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(320px,.85fr);gap:48px;align-items:center}.secondary-media-grid h1{font-size:clamp(38px,4.6vw,62px)}.secondary-media-grid>div>p{max-width:750px}.secondary-media-grid :global(.process-image){border:1px solid #40516a;background:#14263e}.hero-actions{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:25px;margin-top:30px}.secondary-position,.other-processes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:90px}.secondary-position h2,.other-processes h2{font-size:clamp(36px,4vw,52px);line-height:1.1;margin:16px 0 0;letter-spacing:-1.5px}.secondary-position p,.other-processes p{color:var(--muted)}.secondary-position .lead{color:var(--ink);font-size:20px}.process-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px}.process-grid article{background:#fff;border-top:3px solid var(--orange);padding:28px;scroll-margin-top:30px}.process-grid article>span{font:700 12px var(--display);color:var(--orange);letter-spacing:1px}.process-grid h3{font-size:25px;margin:16px 0 12px}.process-grid p,.process-grid li{color:var(--muted)}.process-grid ul{padding-left:19px;margin:20px 0 0}.process-grid li+li{margin-top:8px}.requirements-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));margin:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.requirements-list div{padding:25px 24px 25px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.requirements-list div:nth-child(even){padding-left:24px;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.requirements-list dt{font-weight:700;margin-bottom:7px}.requirements-list dd{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}.secondary-faq{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;gap:70px}.faq-list details{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:20px 0}.faq-list details:first-child{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.faq-list summary{font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;padding-right:14px}.faq-list details p{color:var(--muted);margin:15px 0 0}summary:focus-visible,.secondary-hero a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--orange);outline-offset:4px}
  @media(max-width:800px){.process-grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.secondary-position,.other-processes{gap:40px}.secondary-faq{gap:30px}}
  @media(max-width:900px){.secondary-media-grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:36px}}
  @media(max-width:700px){.hero-actions{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}.secondary-position,.other-processes,.requirements-list,.secondary-faq{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.secondary-position,.other-processes{gap:22px}.requirements-list div:nth-child(even){padding-left:0;border-left:0}.secondary-faq{gap:0}.process-grid article{padding:24px}}
</style>
